title start
kind: decision
tags: decision notes
Decision page: keep every note as a plain text file
title end

paragraph start
Use a decision page when you choose between options and want the reason to survive. This one is a worked example, so replace its text with your own.
paragraph end

section start
title start
Context
title end

paragraph start
Notes were spread over three apps, each with its own format. Searching meant opening every app, and an export could lose structure.
answer start
for: q552a83
asked: What forces this decision now?
Searching and exporting were already failing, and the pile grows every week.
answer end
paragraph end

comment start
Keep the context short and factual. A stranger should understand it a year from now.
comment end
section end

section start
title start
Options
title end

paragraph start
Stay with the three apps. Move everything to one plain text format. Use a database.
answer start
for: qe8a03e
asked: Which option was rejected, and why?
The database was rejected, because no plain editor opens it and grep cannot read it.
answer end
paragraph end

paragraph start
todo: ask whether pictures need a fourth option
Pictures and tables fit none of these options yet.
paragraph end
section end

section start
title start
Decision
title end

paragraph start
Write every note as a plain text file in one folder, and read it with any editor.
answer start
for: qf9407a
asked: Is it one choice, stated so someone can act on it?
Yes. One folder and one format, with no exceptions.
answer end
paragraph end
section end

section start
title start
Consequences
title end

paragraph start
Search and diffs become simple and nothing is locked in. Pictures and tables need their own answer later.
answer start
for: q0cb6eb
asked: What gets harder because of this decision?
Pictures and tables, and any tool that expects a database.
answer end
paragraph end

paragraph start
todo: done folder created and the first fifty notes moved
The move started the same week.
paragraph end
section end
